Python packages inside the runtime asset
----------------------------------------

The runtime asset (`runtime-cuda-*.zip`, downloaded on first launch) is a
Python environment that includes PyTorch, torchvision, OpenCV, spandrel,
ultralytics, transformers, timm, kornia, basicsr, facexlib and others.
Their licences are listed in `python/runtime-lock-media.txt` (package pins)
and remain those of their respective authors. PyTorch is BSD-3-Clause;
OpenCV is Apache-2.0; ultralytics is AGPL-3.0.

Model weights
-------------

Model weights are never bundled. `python/media_ops/media_catalog.json` lists
each model with its download URL, size and SPDX licence identifier
(`licenseSpdx`). Licences differ per model and include MIT, Apache-2.0,
BSD-3-Clause, AGPL-3.0 and — for BRIA RMBG-1.4 — a non-commercial licence
(`BRIA-1.4-NC`). Users are responsible for complying with each model's terms;
`docs/model-guide.md` shows the licence next to every model.

Fonts, icons and UI dependencies
